# Noma Enterprise workspace

::summary
Noma's enterprise workspace is a modular monolith for **Docs**, **Visuals**, and **Work**, with shared identity, authorization, assets, versioning, relationships, search, notifications, changesets, and audit. This page records what the in-repo kernel implements and what remains a deployment or partner-validation concern.
::

## Implemented in this tree

The `EnterpriseWorkspace` kernel (`src/enterprise/`) is the R0/R1 vertical slice plus executable coverage for later-gate contracts that can be proved without a live IdP, AWS account, or Atlassian tenant.

| Area | What is implemented | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Identity | OIDC adapter interface, SCIM upsert/deprovision, short-lived sessions, revocation | `test/enterprise-workspace.test.ts` |
| Docs | Persistent block/table IDs, visual editor adapter that preserves unknown directives, draft/publish coordinator, source-replacement conflicts | `test/stable-identity.test.ts`, adapter tests |
| Visuals | PaperDOM kernel with server-derived actors, revision preconditions, outlines/alt text, asset scan/quarantine | PaperDOM and asset tests |
| Work | Configurable types/workflows, hierarchy, boards, sprints, worklogs, custom fields, JQL subset, reports, automation dry-run | work-domain tests |
| Agents | Changeset lifecycle, no self-approval, untrusted payload policy, kill switch, outbox | changeset tests |
| Knowledge | Permission-aware search and relations; citations carry resource/block/hash | leakage tests |
| Migration | Inventory dispositions (imported/inaccessible/unsupported/quarantined) | importer tests |
| Operations | SQLite enterprise store, PostgreSQL DDL generator, digest-checked backup/restore, legal hold, tamper-evident audit chain | backup and hold tests |
| E2E | Section 17 demonstration: two humans, one agent, connector, pin, stale apply, revocation, restore | `test/enterprise-e2e.test.ts` |

## Not claimed as production-ready

The following remain **outside** this kernel's passing tests and must not be advertised as shipped enterprise capabilities:

- Hosted Tiptap/Yjs CRDT replication across real browsers
- Pinned PaperDOM packages extracted from the standalone PaperDOM repository
- Live Confluence/Jira Cloud or Data Center API adapters (fixtures only)
- Bedrock/EU reference deployment, KMS, malware-scanning products, and independent security assessment
- Usability benchmarks against a partner's configured Confluence/Jira
- Paid-pilot commercial validation

SQLite remains the technical-preview datastore. PostgreSQL is the documented enterprise target; `enterpriseSchema("postgres")` emits JSONB/BYTEA DDL for that migration, and application backup/restore is tested independently of RDS snapshots.

## Package map

Code currently lives under `src/enterprise/` and `src/stable-identity.ts` rather than a one-shot repository split. Target boundaries in the implementation plan remain: `packages/document-core`, `document-ui`, `platform`, `work`, `knowledge`, `connectors`, `contracts`, plus PaperDOM `packages/core|react|io`. Extraction requires golden tests before moves.
